---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import PageIntro from '../../components/PageIntro.astro';
import { site } from '../../lib/config';
---
<Layout lang="en" title="Getting started with Stille" description="Install Stille for Android, exchange profile or one-time invites, and troubleshoot peer-to-peer connections." canonical="/en/guide/">
<Header />
<main id="main" tabindex="-1" class="document-page wrap">
  <PageIntro label="Getting started" title="Your first conversation" description="Install Stille on both devices. Choose a name and exchange an invite — no phone number required." />
  <div class="guide-intro"><div class="prose"><h2>First launch</h2><p>Download the APK, install it, then choose your language, name and theme. Contacts can see your name; you can change it in your profile.</p><a class="text-link" href="/en/download/">Download and install →</a></div><img src="/assets/owl-invite.svg" width="190" height="177" alt="Owl holding an invitation" /></div>
  <section class="guide-section" aria-labelledby="invites-heading"><div class="section-heading"><h2 id="invites-heading">Invites</h2><p>Don't post active invite codes publicly.<br/>Share them only with the intended person.</p></div><div class="guide-columns"><div class="prose"><h3>To invite someone</h3><ol class="instructions"><li>Open Add contact in Chats or Contacts.</li><li>Create a one-time invite, or share your persistent profile link.</li><li>Send its link or show the QR code in person.</li></ol></div><div class="prose"><h3>To accept an invite</h3><ol class="instructions"><li>Open the full HTTPS invite link on Android with Stille installed.</li><li>Profile links use <code>/invite/i/</code> or <code>/invite/i3/</code>; the app handles the code locally.</li><li>If the app does not open, scan the HTTPS QR with Stille's built-in scanner.</li></ol></div></div><p class="notice">The site does not store or resolve profile codes. Availability of Android App Links depends on the installed app version and domain verification.</p></section>
  <section class="document-grid guide-section" aria-labelledby="connection-heading"><div><h2 id="connection-heading">Connection troubleshooting</h2><p class="section-description">Peer-to-peer messaging needs a route between devices.</p></div><div class="prose"><h3>Same local network</h3><p>Invites without an address rely on local discovery. Both devices need the same network with multicast allowed and client isolation disabled.</p><h3>Different networks</h3><p>A reachable address or relay may be required. Internet access alone does not guarantee a direct connection: NAT, firewalls and network policies can interfere.</p><h3>Invite not accepted</h3><p>Make sure the entire invite was received. The app checks validity and use; ask the sender for a new invite if needed.</p><a href={site.android} rel="noreferrer">Android client documentation ↗</a></div></section>
  <section class="faq-section" aria-labelledby="faq-heading"><div><h2 id="faq-heading">Frequently asked questions</h2></div><div class="faq-list"><details><summary>Does Stille need my phone number?</summary><p>No. You choose a name when setting up your profile.</p></details><details><summary>Does this site connect devices?</summary><p>No. Stille connects devices over an available peer-to-peer route.</p></details><details><summary>Where can I report a problem?</summary><p>Open an <a href={`${site.android}/issues`}>issue on GitHub</a>. Include your app version and steps to reproduce, but never share active invite codes or private messages.</p></details></div></section>
</main><Footer />
</Layout>
